Third-party code redistributed in this repository
=================================================

Four files under `src/newt/live/` are adapted from someone else's work and carry
their copyright. Both licences that work is offered under require the licence
text and the copyright notice to travel with any copy, so both texts are in
`licenses/` and both ship inside the wheel — the adapted files are shipped as
package data, which means every install is a redistribution.

  src/newt/live/page/index.html   the embedded-viewer page
  src/newt/live/page/app.js       the focus patch, the viewer options, the import
  src/newt/live/page/view.css     the canvas sizing rule
  src/newt/live/_assets.py        the version pin, the file names, the routing

  Upstream:   https://github.com/mission-robotics-ai/so100-hackathon
              (a fork of https://github.com/rerun-io/so100-hackathon)
  Copyright:  Rerun Technologies AB <opensource@rerun.io>
  Licence:    MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option

  Texts:      licenses/LICENSE-MIT.rerun      (verbatim from upstream)
              licenses/LICENSE-APACHE.rerun   (verbatim from upstream)

Each of those four files names the upstream, the copyright holder and the licence
pair in its own header, and says which parts are theirs and which are ours. Those
headers are the attribution; this file and `licenses/` are the licence text the
attribution was never a substitute for.

`rerun-sdk` itself is a declared dependency of the `[view]` extra, not vendored
code — pip installs it, and it carries its own licence metadata.


newt's own licence
------------------

Not declared. This repository has no LICENSE file and `pyproject.toml` carries no
`license` field, so nothing here states the terms newt is offered under, and this
file does not invent them: choosing a licence for a public SDK is a decision with
consequences for everyone who installs it, and it belongs to whoever owns the
project rather than to whoever last edited it.

What that means in practice, said plainly rather than left to be discovered: an
outside reader has no stated permission to use, copy or modify newt, whatever the
repository's visibility suggests. The absence above is the only honest reading of
that, and the reason it is written down here is so the gap is visible rather than
inferred.

Nothing in this file affects the third-party terms above. Rerun's code is licensed
by Rerun, and those terms hold whatever newt's own turn out to be.
